In article <C40MJI.5yE@eskimo.com> gregs@eskimo.com (Greg Sumner) writes:

>I'm at the castle now.  I have the Heart of What's-his-name and the silver
>bell.  Now what?!  I teleported down to 50 and killed everything.  I
>drank a cursed potion of gain level and I found myself back at the castle.
>My pet Archon didn't manage to follow me back up this time.

	You weren't on 50th level.  In version 3.1, a level-teleport
discontinuity was added, so you can't teleport to any level below the
castle except the first unless you're already below the castle.  You
were only one level below the castle, and the potion you drank only
bears that out.

>I've cleared the Quest, and have discovered the neat trick that the 
>Heart does.  Guess that's one more ring I can drop.  But where do I find
>this Candleabrum and the Book?  What's my next step?

	The Book and Candelabrum lie yet further down.  Go to the rear
of the castle and jump into one of the trap doors, then go to the
temple in the Valley of the Dead and search for doors until you find a
staircase leading down.

	The Book is being held by the Wizard.  Find a small room in
the middle of one of the mazes surrounded by a moat and containing a
...ic portal.  The Candelabrum is being held by Vlad the Impaler in a
small sub-dungeon (like the Gnome mines).  Look for a level with two
up staircases.  Once you have all three, go to the bottom of the
dungeon (deeper than level 50) and wait for further instructions.

